Jim and company,

`fs` is an awesome package. I use it a ton. I love it.

Here's a function, `file_open()` that might be a nice addition that I use quite a bit in my course to open files (e.g. PDF, images, etc) from R. 

Try it out. See if you become addicted as I did. If so, feel free to use it in `fs`. 

``` {r}
file_open <- function(path) {
    
    open_path_chr <- paste0("open '", path, "'")
    
    return(system(open_path_chr))
    
}
```

To match `path_rel()`

```R
path_abs <- function(path, start = ".") {
  if (is_absolute_path(path)) {
    path
  } else {
    fs::path_abs(path(start, path))
  }
}
```

Something like:

```R
path_package <- function(package, ...) {
  system.file(path(...), package = package, mustWork = TRUE)
} 
```

Came from Slack conversation about sanitizing filenames. Example: you want to download a file and create local filename from the remote file (or a Content-Disposition header), but safely.

@jcheng5 pointed to this as a decent place to start:

https://www.npmjs.com/package/sanitize-filename
